{"content_hash": "3101e6c814315593", "version_id": 457, "article_id": 46, "level_code": "ja_n4", "lang": "ja", "level": 2, "level_label": "N4 初級", "title": "パナマで大きな地震、建物がこわれた", "title_zh": "巴拿马发生强震，多栋建筑倒塌", "has_translation": true, "topic": "world", "source": "bbc_world", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c620r39zdp9wo?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1677233860259-ce1a8e0f8498?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8MXx8cG93ZXJmdWwlMjBtYWduaXR1ZGUlMjBlYXJ0aHF1YWtlfGVufDB8MHx8fDE3OTE1OTQ2NTJ8MA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Çağlar Oskay on Unsplash", "author": "Çağlar Oskay", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@oskaycaglar?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/a-car-is-parked-in-front-of-a-destroyed-building-mmLtohu4qmE?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(73, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(111, 46%, 48%)", "label": "WORLD", "seed": "69c1918b4164"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-09", "word_count": 158, "reading_minutes": 0.5, "lead": "パナマで大きい地震がありました。建物がこわれて、たくさんの人が外に出ました。けがをした人の話はまだありません。", "lead_zh": "巴拿马发生了大地震。建筑物被震坏，很多人跑到外面。目前还没有人受伤的消息。", "preview": "金曜日の午後3時ごろ、パナマでマグニチュード7.7の地震がありました。震えはとても強く、約460万人が感じました。地震の場所はパナマの中南部で、町の近くでした。", "preview_zh": "周五下午3点左右，巴拿马发生了7.7级地震。震动非常强烈，大约460万人有震感。震中位于巴拿马中南部，在一个小镇附近。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 447, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/46/ja_n4.mp3", "duration": 33.425, "size_bytes": 204336, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "ja-JP-NanamiNeural", "word_count": 105, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@fc48a26/content/data/versions/457.json", "paragraphs": ["金曜日の午後3時ごろ、パナマでマグニチュード7.7の地震がありました。震えはとても強く、約460万人が感じました。地震の場所はパナマの中南部で、町の近くでした。", "インターネットの映像では、いくつかの建物がこわれていました。ペノノメという町では、教会の一部が落ちました。ホテルもほとんどこわれました。今のところ、死んだ人やけがをした人の話はありません。"], "paragraphs_zh": ["周五下午3点左右，巴拿马发生了7.7级地震。震动非常强烈，大约460万人有震感。震中位于巴拿马中南部，在一个小镇附近。", "网上的视频显示，好几栋建筑被震坏。在佩诺诺梅镇，一座教堂的部分建筑掉了下来。一家酒店也几乎完全倒塌。目前还没有人员死亡或受伤的消息。"], "body": "金曜日の午後3時ごろ、パナマでマグニチュード7.7の地震がありました。震えはとても強く、約460万人が感じました。地震の場所はパナマの中南部で、町の近くでした。\n\nインターネットの映像では、いくつかの建物がこわれていました。ペノノメという町では、教会の一部が落ちました。ホテルもほとんどこわれました。今のところ、死んだ人やけがをした人の話はありません。", "body_zh": "周五下午3点左右，巴拿马发生了7.7级地震。震动非常强烈，大约460万人有震感。震中位于巴拿马中南部，在一个小镇附近。\n\n网上的视频显示，好几栋建筑被震坏。在佩诺诺梅镇，一座教堂的部分建筑掉了下来。一家酒店也几乎完全倒塌。目前还没有人员死亡或受伤的消息。", "text": "金曜日の午後3時ごろ、パナマでマグニチュード7.7の地震がありました。震えはとても強く、約460万人が感じました。地震の場所はパナマの中南部で、町の近くでした。 インターネットの映像では、いくつかの建物がこわれていました。ペノノメという町では、教会の一部が落ちました。ホテルもほとんどこわれました。今のところ、死んだ人やけがをした人の話はありません。", "vocab": [{"word": "地震", "pos": "noun", "zh": "地震", "note": "常用词，读作「じしん」"}, {"word": "建物", "pos": "noun", "zh": "建筑物", "note": "读作「たてもの」"}, {"word": "こわれる", "pos": "verb", "zh": "坏掉、倒塌", "note": "自动词，如「建物がこわれる」"}, {"word": "マグニチュード", "pos": "noun", "zh": "震级", "note": "地震大小的单位"}, {"word": "震え", "pos": "noun", "zh": "震动", "note": "读作「ふるえ」"}, {"word": "映像", "pos": "noun", "zh": "影像、视频", "note": "读作「えいぞう」"}, {"word": "教会", "pos": "noun", "zh": "教堂", "note": "读作「きょうかい」"}, {"word": "大統領", "pos": "noun", "zh": "总统", "note": "读作「だいとうりょう」"}, {"word": "運河", "pos": "noun", "zh": "运河", "note": "读作「うんが」"}, {"word": "予定", "pos": "noun", "zh": "预定、计划", "note": "读作「よてい」"}], "title_original": "Powerful magnitude 7.7 earthquake hits Panama, damaging buildings", "summary_original": "Tsunami warnings are issued for neighbouring countries as videos of destruction circulate online.", "body_original": "Powerful magnitude 7.7 earthquake hits Panama, damaging buildings\nBy\nMichael Sheils McNamee\nPublished\n9 October 2026\nA massive magnitude 7.7 earthquake has hit Panama, damaging buildings and causing widespread shaking.\nAbout 4.6 million people felt moderate to severe tremors as a result of the quake, according to the US Geological Survey, which has said that the effects of the quake were \"likely to be widespread\".\nIt struck just before 15:00 local time (18:00 GMT) on Friday, with an epicentre about 6.2 miles (10km) from the town of Pitaloza Arriba in south-central Panama.\nFootage shared online appears to show collapsed buildings in the towns of Penonomé and Soná, including one of a man calling out to anyone trapped under the rubble of a collapsed building. No casualties have so far been reported.\nVerified footage shows one side of a cathedral in Penonomé collapsed due to the shaking, as well as one of its spires.\nAnother video showed a local hotel had almost completely collapsed.\nRicardo Brown, who lives in the southern Herrera province, told news agency Reuters that the earthquake had damaged several homes in his neighbourhood of Las Minas.\n\"We're scared. It's just the two of us old folks here. The house has cracked and we're afraid it could fall on us,\" the 74-year-old said.\nThe full extent of the damage it has caused is not yet clear, though several large aftershocks were also reported near the initial earthquake, potentially complicating the situation on the surface.\nThe quake was registered as occurring at a depth of just 12km. The shallower the earthquake, the more likely it is to have more severe effects on the surface.\nMany people were evacuated from buildings in Panama City, about 200km from the epicentre, and were seen taking to the streets or sitting in nearby parks until the shaking had ceased.\nDamage in the capital appears to be limited to that caused by debris falling from roofs.\nPanama's President José Raúl Mulino said his entire government was mobilising in response to the earthquake, adding: \"What happened should not be used to cause alarm or disorder.\"\nTsunami warnings were initially issued for 11 countries neighbouring Panama, before the US Tsunami Warning System confirmed there was no threat.\nThe Panama Canal - a vital waterway linking the Atlantic and Pacific oceans - was unaffected by the earthquake, the authority that oversees marine traffic through it said.\nThe earthquake comes just three days before Panama was scheduled to hold a national evacuation drill for dealing with a major earthquake.\nIt also follows devastating earthquakes in Colombia and Venezuela earlier this year.\nRelated topics\nMexico\nEarthquakes\nChile\nPanama", "fetched_at": "2026-10-10T01:10:50.719840", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "金曜日", "s": 0.163, "e": 0.713, "sm": 162, "em": 712, "cs": 0, "ce": 3, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "の", "s": 0.725, "e": 0.85, "sm": 725, "em": 850, "cs": 3, "ce": 4, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "午後", "s": 0.863, "e": 1.219, "sm": 862, "em": 1218, "cs": 4, "ce": 6, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "3", "s": 1.219, "e": 1.397, "sm": 1218, "em": 1396, "cs": 6, "ce": 7, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "時", "s": 1.397, "e": 1.575, "sm": 1396, "em": 1575, "cs": 7, "ce": 8, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "ごろ", "s": 1.575, "e": 1.913, "sm": 1575, "em": 1912, "cs": 8, "ce": 10, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "、", "s": 1.913, "e": 2.225, "sm": 1912, "em": 2225, "cs": 10, "ce": 11, "si": 0}, {"i": 7, "w": "パナマ", "s": 2.225, "e": 2.6, "sm": 2225, "em": 2600, "cs": 11, "ce": 14, "si": 0}, {"i": 8, "w": "で", "s": 2.612, "e": 2.75, "sm": 2612, "em": 2750, "cs": 14, "ce": 15, "si": 0}, {"i": 9, "w": "マグニチュード", "s": 2.788, "e": 3.575, "sm": 2787, "em": 3575, "cs": 15, "ce": 22, "si": 0}, {"i": 10, "w": "7.7", "s": 3.587, "e": 4.338, "sm": 3587, "em": 4337, "cs": 22, "ce": 25, "si": 0}, {"i": 11, "w": "の", "s": 4.35, "e": 4.462, "sm": 4350, "em": 4462, "cs": 25, "ce": 26, "si": 0}, {"i": 12, "w": "地震", "s": 4.475, "e": 4.875, "sm": 4475, "em": 4875, "cs": 26, "ce": 28, "si": 0}, {"i": 13, "w": "が", "s": 4.888, "e": 5.0, "sm": 4887, "em": 5000, "cs": 28, "ce": 29, "si": 0}, {"i": 14, "w": "あり", "s": 5.013, "e": 5.2, "sm": 5012, "em": 5200, "cs": 29, "ce": 31, "si": 0}, {"i": 15, "w": "まし", "s": 5.213, "e": 5.438, "sm": 5212, "em": 5437, "cs": 31, "ce": 33, "si": 0}, {"i": 16, "w": "た", "s": 5.45, "e": 